## Marketing review: launch-copy.md vs product/spec.md

### Claims not supported by the spec

| # | Copy claim | Copy text | Spec says | Issue |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | "Works offline, anywhere" | `Works offline, anywhere.` | `Offline support: removed in this release.` | The spec explicitly states offline support is **removed**. The copy wrongly promises it. |
| 2 | Export to **PDF** | `Export to CSV, PDF and Excel in one click.` | `Export: CSV only.` | PDF export is not in the spec. |
| 3 | Export to **Excel** | `Export to CSV, PDF and Excel in one click.` | `Export: CSV only.` | Excel export is not in the spec. |
| 4 | "in one click" | `Export to CSV, PDF and Excel in one click.` | `Export: CSV only.` | The spec limits export to CSV alone; the "one click" bundling of three formats is unsupported. |

### Verdict

Every substantive claim in the launch copy contradicts the product spec. The copy promises offline capability (removed per spec) and three export formats (CSV only per spec). The copy needs a complete rewrite to match the spec.
